# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
#
# dist/ is IGNORED here, unlike ts/dist and ts/dist-test which are committed
# deliberately (see ts/.gitignore). That distinction is the point: ts/ is the
# published SDK, so a consumer reads and runs its compiled form straight from
# a clone. app/ is the demo API server, and nothing consumes its compiled
# form without producing it first. Every entry point builds: `npm test`,
# `npm run test:unit`, `npm run test:integration` and `npm run server` all run
# `tsc` first, scripts/validate-full.sh starts with `npm run build`, the CI
# app job builds before it starts the server, and README/AGENTS both document
# `npm start` as requiring a build. A committed dist/ therefore has no reader,
# only the standing risk that it goes stale and someone runs old code.
#
# It also kept a trap in the drift gate: that gate fails on any untracked file
# in the tree, so a locally built app/dist/test/*.js would report as generator
# drift it has nothing to do with.
dist/

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# IDE / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
